I have enough to answer. Two faults reach the user: currency's pod went down, which breaks checkout's currency calls, and a DNS failure in frontend, which breaks product-reviews calls.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "currency",
      "fault_kind": "pod_unavailable",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT time, attr_k8s_pod_name AS pod, metric, value FROM abnormal_metrics_sum WHERE metric='k8s.container.restarts' AND attr_k8s_pod_name LIKE 'currency%' ORDER BY time", "claim": "Currency pod restart counter rose from 0 to 1 at about 11:38:05, inside the incident window."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, service_name, count(*) n, min(time) t0, max(time) t1 FROM abnormal_traces WHERE span_name LIKE 'Currency%' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "Currency served only 3 spans, all at 11:37:45, versus 14 in the normal period; none after the restart."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT time, span_name, attr_status_code, round(duration/1e6,2) AS ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE span_name='oteldemo.CurrencyService/Convert' AND service_name='checkout' AND attr_status_code='Error' ORDER BY time", "claim": "Checkout's CurrencyService/Convert calls fail with Error status from 11:38:07 onward, each in under 1 ms."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "service": "frontend",
      "fault_kind": "dns_lookup_failed",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, attr_status_code, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE span_name='dns.lookup' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "Frontend dns.lookup client spans errored 3 times in the incident, against 1 in the normal period."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT time, span_name, attr_status_code, round(duration/1e6,2) AS ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend' AND span_name LIKE 'grpc.oteldemo.ProductReviewService/%' ORDER BY time", "claim": "Frontend's ProductReviewService calls fail with Error in under 0.3 ms, from 11:37:33 on, versus none failing in normal period."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {"from": "currency", "to": "checkout", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, attr_status_code, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='checkout' AND span_name IN ('oteldemo.CurrencyService/Convert','oteldemo.CheckoutService/PlaceOrder') GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "Checkout's currency Convert client calls and its PlaceOrder server spans both show 10 errors, while other checkout calls stay clean."}]},
    {"from": "checkout", "to": "frontend", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, attr_http_response_status_code code, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend' AND span_name IN ('POST /api/checkout','grpc.oteldemo.CheckoutService/PlaceOrder') GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "Frontend's PlaceOrder client spans and POST /api/checkout server spans return 500 for the same 11 requests."}]},
    {"from": "frontend", "to": "frontend-proxy", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, attr_http_response_status_code code, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend-proxy' AND attr_status_code='Error' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "Frontend-proxy ingress and egress spans return 500 for about 23 requests, mirroring frontend's failed checkout and product-review calls."}]}
  ]
}
```

